<p>In the latest turn in the widening West Asia war, President Trump said U.S. forces struck military targets on Iran’s Kharg Island, a strategic Persian Gulf outpost that handles most of Iran’s crude exports. U.S. and other reports said the raid targeted military assets on the island, not its oil export infrastructure, while Trump warned that the oil facilities could be attacked if Iran or others interfere with shipping through the Strait of Hormuz. Iranian state media said the island’s oil infrastructure was not damaged. The strike adds a new layer of risk to a conflict now in its third week, with Kharg Island’s role in global energy flows putting oil markets and maritime security at the center of events. Iran’s armed forces responded by warning that any attack on Iran’s oil and energy infrastructure would trigger attacks on energy infrastructure linked to companies cooperating with the United States. One possible stabilizing step came in Trump’s statement that the U.S. Navy would soon begin escorting tankers through the Strait of Hormuz, underscoring efforts to keep one of the world’s key shipping lanes open even as tensions rise.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/obijv_1nIdjPBur67a9S7ifT5tSjZ6-PCwqqIoGYn3qK7pXrauihxF19IhFKnp4TYmhoT7WpU5ZNhg0yN5TELZN9MeuSrn94AWIks36UW-vFX3ENmVu1kAFKrCEds4zCC5fVBrCyX64FwqxX-IXTRHR34iPwk5y2XbplZn6D4SS49eOLud3AgE7bNctLXrrQKMNZ0hXF_P5p_M9FYvT3oCT0klQS7g' alt='A satellite image of Kharg Island in Iran last month.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>What was hit: A U.S. military official said the raid struck military sites on Kharg Island, including locations storing missiles and mines, not economic infrastructure.</li><li>Pressure on markets: Oil prices have risen by more than 40% since the war began, reflecting fears that attacks on export hubs or the Strait of Hormuz could worsen supply disruptions.</li><li>U.S. buildup: The Hindu’s live coverage said the United States was moving additional Marines to the region, pointing to broader military reinforcement beyond the Kharg strike.</li><li>Public signaling: Trump posted bombing footage of the Kharg Island strike after announcing the raid, giving the military action a strong public-messaging component.</li></ul><blockquote>For reasons of decency, I have chosen NOT to wipe out the Oil Infrastructure on the Island. - President Donald Trump</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>United States: President Trump framed the strike as leverage to protect maritime passage, saying he had chosen not to hit Kharg Island’s oil facilities for now and warning that could change if shipping through the Strait of Hormuz is threatened. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/mar/13/trump-military-kharg-island-iran-oil-export'>The Guardian</a>)</li><li>Iranian armed forces: Iran’s military warned that if Iran’s oil and energy infrastructure is attacked, it will strike energy infrastructure belonging to oil companies cooperating with the United States. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/mar/13/iran-war-news-live-updates-us-israel-middle-east-crisis-latest'>The Guardian</a>)</li><li>Financial analysts: Banks cited by the Financial Times said markets were already dealing with a historic supply disruption and warned the conflict could turn into a prolonged energy crisis if export outages persist. (<a href='https://www.ft.com/content/e5d1f192-c9f1-448f-9aa4-528d6e867cd2'>Financial Times</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/kharg-island-the-pearl-of-the-persian-gulf/article70742480.ece'>Kharg Island: The pearl of the Persian Gulf</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/mar/13/trump-military-kharg-island-iran-oil-export'>Trump says US forces destroyed military targets on Iranian island handling oil exports</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='http://www.euronews.com/2026/03/14/trump-says-us-has-totally-obliterated-military-targets-on-irans-kharg-